    "content": "<h2>A Single-Level Retreat in Chandler's Springfield Community</h2>\n<p>If you have been searching for a home that pairs comfortable, single-level living with a true resort-style lifestyle, <strong>6073 S Bedford Place</strong> deserves a close look. This 3-bedroom, 2-bath ranch-style home offers approximately <strong>2,158 square feet</strong> in Chandler's Springfield community, and it is listed at <strong>$560,000</strong>. Built in 1997, the home sits in a neighborhood known for golf, tennis, pickleball, a clubhouse and a full calendar of social activities, making it an appealing choice for buyers who want more from their community than just a street address.</p>\n<p>The home is being sold out of a probate estate, which can create real opportunity for a prepared buyer. It also means careful due diligence matters more than usual, a point we come back to below.</p>\n<h2>Features and Layout</h2>\n<p>The listing describes a beautifully appointed kitchen, attractive bathrooms and flexible living spaces that can work as a den, hobby room, home office or guest retreat. The ranch-style, single-story design keeps everything on one level, which many buyers in this part of Chandler specifically want.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>3 bedrooms and 2 full bathrooms</strong> across roughly 2,158 sq ft</li>\n<li><strong>Kitchen island and pantry</strong> for easy cooking and storage</li>\n<li><strong>9-foot-plus flat ceilings</strong> that give the rooms an open, airy feel</li>\n<li><strong>Spacious primary suite</strong> with a full bath, double vanity and separate shower and tub</li>\n<li><strong>Private yard with fruit trees</strong>, so you can pick fresh fruit right in your own backyard</li>\n<li><strong>2-car garage</strong> and rain gutters</li>\n<li><strong>Forced-air natural gas heating and central air conditioning</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The primary suite is described as a space designed for comfort and relaxation, and the separate shower and tub along with the double vanity make daily routines easier. Flexible living areas give you room to set the home up the way you live, whether that means a formal dining area, a reading room or space for visiting family.</p>\n<h2>The Springfield Lifestyle</h2>\n<p>The biggest selling point here may be the community itself. According to the listing, Springfield residents enjoy <strong>golf, pickleball, tennis, swimming, a spa, a clubhouse</strong> and a variety of social clubs and activities. Springfield is widely known as an active-adult community, so buyers should confirm any age-related occupancy rules and review the HOA documents during their due diligence period.</p>\n<p>Beyond the gates, southeast Chandler (85249) offers some of the most convenient living in the East Valley. You are close to grocery stores, restaurants and medical offices along the Gilbert Road and Riggs Road corridors, and the Loop 202 Santan Freeway gives you quick access to the rest of the Valley and Phoenix Sky Harbor. Nearby parks, golf courses and the shopping and dining scene in downtown Chandler add even more to do.</p>\n<h2>Market Context: Is This a Good Value?</h2>\n<p>At $560,000 for about 2,158 square feet, this home is priced at roughly <strong>$260 per square foot</strong>. For a single-level home in an amenity-rich southeast Chandler community, that is a competitive number, especially compared with newer construction in the area, which often carries a higher price per square foot and smaller lots. Probate sales can sometimes be priced to move because the estate wants to settle, but they can also come with limited seller knowledge about the property's history.</p>\n<p>The listing notes that the family representative never lived in the home and that buyers should verify all information during their due diligence. That makes a thorough home inspection, a careful review of the HOA documents and a close look at title especially important here.</p>\n<h2>Why Buy With Camelback Home Group</h2>\n<p>Probate and estate sales are exactly the kind of transaction where legal oversight pays off. At <strong>Camelback Home Group</strong>, every transaction is backed by <strong>attorney and paralegal oversight</strong>. We review the purchase contract, the probate documents and the personal representative's authority to sell, along with the inspection reports, HOA disclosures and title commitment, so you understand exactly what you are buying and can negotiate with confidence. Most brokerages simply do not offer that level of protection.</p>\n<h2>Schedule Your Showing</h2>\n<p>A single-level home with fruit trees, a spacious primary suite and access to a full resort-style lifestyle in Chandler will not last long at this price. <strong>Call Camelback Home Group at (480) 203-3039</strong> or <a href=\"/#contact\">reach out online</a> to schedule a private showing of 6073 S Bedford Place or to ask any questions about the property, the probate process or the Springfield community.</p>",
