    "excerpt": "A single-level 3-bedroom, 3-bath Troon North home on an approximately 11,497 sq ft lot backing to Natural Area Open Space, listed at $875,000. Two ensuite primary bedrooms, a heated pool and spa, and a 3-car garage are offered in an as-is estate sale with disclosed moisture and mold conditions, a value opportunity for a buyer ready to renovate.",
    "metaDescription": "11139 E Monument Drive, Scottsdale AZ 85262: 3 bed, 3 bath, 2,421 sq ft Troon North estate sale with pool, spa and open-space views, listed at $875,000.",
    "content": "<h2>A Private Troon North Setting With Room to Make It Your Own</h2><p>Some North Scottsdale homes sell on finishes. <strong>11139 E Monument Drive</strong> sells on location, privacy and potential. Set in Pinnacle Views at Troon North, this single-level home sits on a lot of approximately 11,497 square feet. The south-facing backyard backs to Natural Area Open Space and a natural desert wash. It has 3 bedrooms, 3 full bathrooms, 2,421 square feet and a 3-car garage, and it is listed at <strong>$875,000</strong>. That is an unusual entry point into one of Scottsdale's best-known golf and desert communities.</p><p>The home is being sold as an <strong>estate sale in AS-IS, WHERE-IS condition</strong>. The listing discloses known moisture intrusion and mold-related conditions that need attention. This is a home for a buyer who is ready to take on improvements, and it rewards careful due diligence. We cover that below.</p><h2>Layout and Interior Features</h2><p>The 1997 home uses a <strong>split-bedroom floor plan</strong> built around two large ensuite primary bedrooms. Each one has a big walk-in closet, which makes the plan a good fit for multigenerational living, long-term guests or two people who want their own space. One primary suite opens directly to the pool and spa. A third bedroom and a separate full bathroom complete the sleeping wing.</p><ul><li><strong>Travertine stone flooring</strong> in the main living areas</li><li>Kitchen with <strong>granite countertops</strong>, a kitchen island, breakfast bar, eat-in dining area and pantry</li><li>Living and dining areas with a <strong>fireplace</strong> and views of the backyard</li><li>Primary bath with double vanity and separate shower and tub</li><li>No interior steps: true single-level living</li><li>Central air with ceiling fans, plus high-speed internet</li><li>Attached <strong>3-car garage</strong></li></ul><h2>Outdoor Living Against the Sonoran Desert</h2><p>The backyard is where this property stands out. An <strong>expansive covered patio</strong> looks over a heated outdoor pool and spa. A built-in BBQ makes it easy to host. Because the yard backs to protected open space and a desert wash, there are no rear neighbors, and mature desert plants frame the view. In North Scottsdale's cooler months, a yard like this becomes a second living room.</p><p>Some recent exterior work has also been done. According to the listing, <strong>November 2026 improvements</strong> include exterior paint, stucco and parapet repairs, and a professional recoat of the flat roof.</p><h2>Buying an As-Is Estate Property: Know Before You Offer</h2><p>The seller has disclosed moisture and mold-related conditions. Inspection findings, remediation information and the Seller's Property Disclosure Statement are in the MLS documents. A smart buyer will:</p><ul><li>Review every disclosure and prior inspection report before writing an offer</li><li>Schedule their own independent inspection, including a mold and moisture assessment</li><li>Get remediation and repair bids during the inspection period</li><li>Understand how an as-is estate sale affects repair requests and contract terms</li></ul><p>This is where <strong>Camelback Home Group's attorney and paralegal oversight</strong> makes a real difference. On an estate sale with disclosed conditions, the purchase contract, inspection-period timing, disclosure review and title work all matter more than usual. Our team reviews these documents with legal precision, so you know exactly what you are buying and what your options are, at no added cost to you.</p><h2>Troon North and North Scottsdale Living</h2><p>Troon North is known for its <strong>two championship golf courses</strong>, the Monument and the Pinnacle, set against Pinnacle Peak and boulder-strewn desert. Residents are minutes from the trailheads of the <strong>McDowell Sonoran Preserve</strong>, one of the largest urban preserves in the country, and from Pinnacle Peak Park. Shopping and dining at The Shops at Troon North, Pinnacle Peak and the Scottsdale Road corridor are close by, and the Loop 101 connects to the rest of the Valley. The 85262 zip code offers dark skies, quiet streets and desert views, and it remains one of Scottsdale's most desirable addresses.</p><h2>Market Context: Is This a Good Value?</h2><p>At $875,000 for 2,421 square feet, the home is listed at about <strong>$361 per square foot</strong>. That is well below what updated single-level homes in Troon North usually bring. The discount reflects the disclosed condition and the work ahead. For a buyer with a clear repair budget and realistic expectations, this is a chance to buy a premium lot backing to open space, with a pool, a spa and a 3-car garage, at a price that leaves room to renovate. The key is knowing your total cost before you commit, and that is exactly what our process is built for.</p><h2>Schedule a Showing</h2><p>If you want a Troon North address and are open to a project, 11139 E Monument Drive, Scottsdale, AZ 85262 deserves a close look. <strong>Call Camelback Home Group at (480) 203-3039</strong> or <a href=\"/#contact\">contact our team online</a>. We can set up a private showing, walk you through the disclosure package and help you structure a well-protected offer.</p>"
