    "metaDescription": "5-bed, 4-bath Cave Creek home on 1.1 acres with a guest apartment, home office, detached 3-car garage, workshop, RV gate and no HOA, listed at $890,000.",
    "content": "<h2>Space, Privacy and Flexibility in Cave Creek</h2>\n<p>If you've been looking for room to breathe without moving to the middle of nowhere, <strong>5518 E Seven Palms Drive</strong> deserves a close look. Set back from the road on a <strong>1.1-acre north/south lot with mountain views</strong>, this Cave Creek property offers <strong>5 bedrooms, 4 bathrooms and 3,450 square feet under roof</strong>, a separate guest apartment, a detached 3-car garage, a workshop, an RV gate and <strong>no HOA</strong>. It's listed at <strong>$890,000</strong>.</p>\n<p>The seller is clear that the home is being sold <strong>\"as is\"</strong> and that the price reflects it. For buyers who want acreage, outbuildings and income or multigenerational potential, and who are ready to put their own stamp on the kitchen, that's an opportunity.</p>\n\n<h2>Main Home, Guest Apartment and Home Office</h2>\n<p>The main home has <strong>four bedrooms and 2.75 baths</strong>, a living room with a fireplace and a formal dining room. One feature stands out for anyone who works from home: a <strong>large office with its own entrance</strong>, well suited to a home business or client visits without sending people through your living space.</p>\n<p>On the northwest corner of the home, a <strong>separate guest apartment</strong> has its own entrance, a great room with a kitchen, a good-size bedroom, a full bath and storage. It works as guest quarters, a place for aging parents or adult children, or a potential rental (buyers should confirm local rules before renting it out).</p>\n<p>From the MLS listing:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>1.1-acre lot</strong> with N/S exposure, mountain views and natural desert landscaping</li>\n<li><strong>No HOA</strong>, so you have more freedom to use the land the way you want</li>\n<li>Separate <strong>guest apartment</strong> with kitchen, bedroom, full bath and private entrance</li>\n<li><strong>Home office with its own entrance</strong></li>\n<li>Newer <strong>detached 3-car garage</strong> and a newer detached <strong>12' x 14' workshop</strong></li>\n<li><strong>RV gate</strong> on the west end of the garage with room for a boat, RV or extra vehicles, plus additional guest parking</li>\n<li>Fully fenced back area and a back patio with a <strong>beehive fireplace</strong></li>\n<li>Kitchen island, breakfast bar, pantry and 9-foot-plus flat ceilings, with no interior steps</li>\n<li>Many furniture pieces available by separate bill of sale</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Why Cave Creek</h2>\n<p>Cave Creek has a character all its own. The town is known for its <strong>Western heritage, open desert and relaxed pace</strong>, but it's also, as the listing puts it, an area that's \"exciting and vibrant.\" Cave Creek Road and the town core offer local restaurants, saloons, galleries and shops, and the community calendar stays busy with festivals and events.</p>\n<p>Outdoor recreation is close at hand. <strong>Cave Creek Regional Park</strong> and <strong>Spur Cross Ranch Conservation Area</strong> offer hiking, horseback riding and wildflower views, and the Tonto National Forest is just to the north. When you need the city, Carefree Highway and the Loop 101 put North Phoenix, Desert Ridge and Scottsdale within easy reach.</p>\n\n<h2>Market Context: Is This a Good Value?</h2>\n<p>At about <strong>$258 per square foot</strong>, this property is priced well below what many North Valley buyers pay for newer homes on standard lots, and the price includes an acre-plus parcel, a guest apartment, a newer garage, a workshop and RV parking. Properties with this mix of features and no HOA are hard to find in the Cave Creek and Carefree area.</p>\n<p>The trade-off is condition. Built in <strong>1970</strong> and offered as is, the home will likely call for updates, starting with the kitchen. Smart buyers will budget for renovation, get thorough inspections (including septic, well or water service, roof and HVAC, as applicable), and compare the all-in cost to move-in-ready homes nearby. Done right, a property like this can build real equity.</p>\n\n<h2>Attorney and Paralegal Oversight on Every Deal</h2>\n<p>As-is sales, acreage, separate living quarters and outbuildings all raise questions that a typical buyer may not think to ask. At <strong>Camelback Home Group</strong>, every transaction is backed by <strong>attorney and paralegal oversight</strong>. We review the contract, seller disclosures, title and any recorded easements, help you use your inspection period wisely, and make sure items like the furniture bill of sale are documented properly, all so you can buy with confidence.</p>\n\n<h2>Schedule a Showing</h2>\n<p>Ready to see what you'd do with this property? Call the Camelback Home Group team at <strong>(480) 203-3039</strong> to schedule a showing of 5518 E Seven Palms Drive, ask about renovation and financing options, or request comparable sales in Cave Creek.</p>"
