    "content": "<h2>A Five-Bedroom Pool Home in North Phoenix's Arizona Hillcrest</h2>\n<p>3205 W Quail Track Drive is a <strong>5-bedroom, 3-bathroom</strong> home in the <strong>Arizona Hillcrest</strong> neighborhood of North Phoenix, listed at <strong>$650,000</strong>. Built in 2002, it offers <strong>3,062 square feet</strong> of living space, a loft, a <strong>3-car garage</strong> and a fenced backyard with a diving pool and mountain views. It also comes with something buyers rarely see right now: a <strong>VA assumable loan opportunity</strong>.</p>\n<p>That combination of size, a resort-style yard, recent exterior updates and a possible below-market interest rate makes this one of the more interesting North Phoenix listings to come on the market this month.</p>\n\n<h2>Layout and Interior Features</h2>\n<p>The home is built around a formal dining room, an impressive staircase and an updated kitchen. According to the MLS listing, interior highlights include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Updated eat-in kitchen</strong> with granite counters, a center island and a pantry</li>\n<li><strong>Formal dining room</strong> for holidays and larger gatherings</li>\n<li><strong>Downstairs bedroom with a full bath</strong>, a good fit for guests, an office or multigenerational living</li>\n<li><strong>Upstairs primary suite</strong> with dual closets and an updated bath with a double vanity, separate tub and walk-in shower</li>\n<li>Three more upstairs bedrooms plus a <strong>loft</strong> for a playroom, media space or second office</li>\n<li>Plantation shutters, 9-foot-plus flat ceilings and ceiling fans</li>\n<li>Natural gas heat and central air</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Having a full bedroom and bath on the ground floor matters more than many buyers expect. It lets visiting parents, older kids or long-term guests have their own space without climbing stairs.</p>\n\n<h2>An Entertainer's Backyard</h2>\n<p>The backyard is where this home stands out. It has a <strong>fenced diving pool with a slide</strong>, an extended covered patio, low-maintenance artificial turf, raised garden beds and a fruit tree, all with mountain views. The pool fencing is a real plus for families with young children.</p>\n<p>The property also has an <strong>RV gate</strong> and parking for six vehicles, which is hard to find in North Phoenix. That makes it a good option for buyers with a boat, trailer, RV or several drivers in the house.</p>\n\n<h2>Recent Updates</h2>\n<p>Several of the big-ticket items buyers worry about have already been handled:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>New roof (2023)</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Fresh exterior paint (2024)</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Backyard irrigation (2026)</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>A newer roof and recent paint mean fewer surprises during inspection and lower costs in the first years of ownership.</p>\n\n<h2>The VA Assumable Loan Opportunity</h2>\n<p>The listing advertises a <strong>VA assumable loan</strong>. Under an assumption, a qualified buyer may be able to take over the seller's existing mortgage, possibly at an interest rate well below today's rates. That can lower the monthly payment significantly. Assumptions do have conditions: the buyer usually has to qualify with the loan servicer, cover the gap between the loan balance and the purchase price, and understand how the seller's VA entitlement is affected. These deals take more paperwork and a longer timeline than a standard purchase, so it helps to have a team that knows the process.</p>\n\n<h2>Living in North Phoenix</h2>\n<p>This part of North Phoenix (85083) offers quick access to <strong>I-17 and the Loop 101</strong>, so commutes to Deer Valley, Downtown Phoenix and the West Valley are easy. <strong>Norterra</strong> shopping and dining are nearby, and so is the fast-growing <strong>TSMC</strong> semiconductor campus, one of the largest employment projects in the state. The area has easy access to parks and hiking trails, including the Sonoran Preserve trail system, and the home is served by the <strong>Deer Valley Unified School District</strong>.</p>\n\n<h2>Is This Home a Good Value?</h2>\n<p>At $650,000 for 3,062 square feet, this home is priced at about <strong>$212 per square foot</strong>. That is competitive for a five-bedroom pool home in North Phoenix with a 3-car garage, RV gate and recent roof. The possible VA assumption is the bigger story. For a buyer who qualifies, assuming a lower-rate loan could change the monthly cost far more than a small change in price would. Our team can help you compare an assumption with conventional financing so you can see the real numbers.</p>\n\n<h2>Buy With Legal Oversight From Camelback Home Group</h2>\n<p>At <strong>Camelback Home Group</strong>, every transaction is backed by <strong>attorney and paralegal oversight</strong>. That matters even more on a loan assumption, where the documents, servicer approval and closing timeline need careful attention. We review contract terms, inspection findings, HOA documents and title work before you sign, so you understand exactly what you are agreeing to.</p>\n\n<h2>Schedule a Showing</h2>\n<p>Ready to see 3205 W Quail Track Drive or learn more about the VA assumable loan? <strong>Call Camelback Home Group at (480) 203-3039</strong> or contact us online to schedule a private showing. We will walk you through the home, the neighborhood and your financing options.</p>"
