    "content": "<h2>A Five-Bedroom Pool Home in Smith Farms</h2>\n<p>40324 W Art Place is a <strong>5-bedroom, 3-bathroom</strong> home in Maricopa's <strong>Smith Farms</strong> neighborhood, listed at <strong>$399,000</strong>. Built in 2006, it offers <strong>2,920 square feet</strong> of living space on a <strong>10,377 square foot lot</strong>, with a private pool, a covered patio and a <strong>3-car garage</strong>. Five bedrooms, a pool and a lot over 10,000 square feet are hard to find together in this price range anywhere in the Phoenix metro.</p>\n<p>For buyers who need room for a large household, guests who stay for weeks at a time, or a dedicated home office, this house covers a lot of ground for the money.</p>\n\n<h2>Layout and Interior Features</h2>\n<p>The most practical part of the floor plan is the <strong>first-floor bedroom with a full bathroom</strong>. That setup works well for multigenerational living, visiting family, or a private office that sits away from the main bedrooms upstairs. With five bedrooms in total, there is room to set aside one or two for flex use and still give everyone their own space.</p>\n<p>The kitchen is built for everyday cooking and for hosting:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Granite countertops</strong> with plenty of prep space</li>\n<li><strong>Stainless steel appliances</strong></li>\n<li>A <strong>gas cooktop</strong>, which serious home cooks tend to prefer</li>\n<li><strong>Abundant cabinet storage</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The home is heated with natural gas and cooled by central air with ceiling fans. According to the listing, the <strong>air conditioning unit serving the first floor is newer</strong>. In a two-zone home in the Arizona heat, a newer unit on one floor is worth noting during your inspection.</p>\n\n<h2>Backyard, Pool and Garage</h2>\n<p>The backyard is where this property stands out. It has a <strong>private pool</strong>, a <strong>covered patio</strong> for shade, and an <strong>oversized yard</strong> with room for outdoor dining, play space or gardening. In Maricopa, where many newer homes sit on compact lots, a yard of this size is a real advantage.</p>\n<p>The <strong>3-car garage</strong> leaves room for two vehicles plus storage, a workshop or a golf cart.</p>\n\n<h2>A Note on the Leased Solar</h2>\n<p>The listing states the home has <strong>leased solar</strong>. Leased solar can lower monthly electric bills, but the lease usually has to be transferred to the buyer, and the solar company typically must approve that transfer. Before closing, a buyer should review the remaining term, the monthly payment, any escalator clause, buyout options, and what happens if the panels need to come off for roof work. Lenders may also ask about the lease during underwriting. This is the kind of document review our team handles as part of every transaction.</p>\n\n<h2>Living in Maricopa</h2>\n<p>Maricopa is one of the fastest-growing cities in Pinal County, and many buyers choose it because they get more house and more land for the money than in much of the Phoenix metro. Smith Farms is an established neighborhood with mature streets and homes, a good fit for buyers who would rather not live in an active construction zone.</p>\n<p>Residents enjoy:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Copper Sky Regional Park</strong>, with a lake, sports fields, trails and a multigenerational recreation center</li>\n<li>Shopping, dining and services along the <strong>John Wayne Parkway (SR-347)</strong> corridor</li>\n<li>Entertainment at <strong>Harrah's Ak-Chin</strong> and the nearby Ak-Chin community</li>\n<li>An <strong>Amtrak station</strong> and growing local employment and retail</li>\n<li>Access to Chandler, Tempe and Phoenix via SR-347 and Interstate 10</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The city has a small-town feel, open desert views and a strong sense of community, while the job centers of the East Valley and Phoenix are within reach.</p>\n\n<h2>Is It a Good Value?</h2>\n<p>At $399,000 for 2,920 square feet, this home is priced at roughly <strong>$137 per square foot</strong>. That is well below what buyers typically pay per square foot for newer construction in Maricopa, and far below the Phoenix metro average. Add the pool, the 10,377 square foot lot and the 3-car garage, and the value is clear.</p>\n<p>As with any 2006 home, a buyer should budget for a thorough inspection, with particular attention to the roof, the second-floor AC unit, the water heater and the pool equipment. Factoring the solar lease payment into your monthly budget will also give you a true picture of ownership costs.</p>\n\n<h2>Buy With Attorney and Paralegal Oversight</h2>\n<p>Camelback Home Group is not a typical brokerage. Every transaction we handle is overseen by an <strong>attorney and a paralegal</strong>, which means your purchase contract, inspection response, HOA documents, and any solar lease transfer get a careful legal review before you sign. For a home like this, where a solar agreement goes along with the purchase, that extra layer of protection matters.</p>\n\n<h2>Schedule a Showing</h2>\n<p>A home with five bedrooms, a pool and a large lot at this price is likely to draw strong interest. To tour 40324 W Art Place, call Camelback Home Group at <strong>(480) 203-3039</strong> or contact us online. We will set up a showing, pull recent comparable sales in Smith Farms, and help you write a strong, well-protected offer.</p>"
