    "excerpt": "A single-level 3-bed, 2-bath Fountain Hills home on a fenced quarter-acre lot with no HOA or NPOA, listed at $465,000. It has vaulted ceilings, a wood-burning fireplace, mountain and fountain views, and a 2023 HVAC replacement.",
    "metaDescription": "Tour 13825 N Kendall Drive in Fountain Hills, AZ: a single-level 3-bed, 2-bath home on a 9,800 sq ft lot with no HOA, minutes from Fountain Park, listed at $465,000.",
    "content": "<h2>Single-Level Living in the Heart of Fountain Hills</h2>\n<p>13825 N Kendall Drive is a <strong>3-bedroom, 2-bathroom</strong> single-level home in Fountain Hills, listed at <strong>$465,000</strong>. Built in 1993, it offers <strong>1,366 square feet</strong> of living space, a <strong>2-car garage</strong> and a fully fenced lot of about <strong>9,800 square feet</strong>. It also has <strong>no HOA and no NPOA</strong>, which is unusual in this part of the Valley and means no monthly association dues and fewer restrictions on how you use the property.</p>\n<p>Fountain Hills homes under $500,000 are scarce. Few come with a quarter-acre lot, a covered patio with mountain and fountain views, and a long list of recent updates.</p>\n\n<h2>Layout and Interior Features</h2>\n<p>The open floor plan is bright and comfortable. Highlights include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Vaulted ceilings</strong> that make the living area feel larger than its square footage</li>\n<li>A <strong>bay window</strong> that brings in plenty of natural light</li>\n<li>A <strong>wood-burning fireplace</strong> for cool desert evenings</li>\n<li>A <strong>large dining area</strong> and a well laid-out kitchen with a <strong>breakfast bar</strong> and plentiful cabinets</li>\n<li>A <strong>split primary suite</strong> with a full bath and double vanity, separated from the two guest bedrooms for privacy</li>\n<li>Full bathrooms with <strong>skylights</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Spanish-style home is heated and cooled by an ENERGY STAR heat pump system, and high-speed internet is available, which helps anyone who works from home.</p>\n\n<h2>A Well-Maintained Home With Recent Updates</h2>\n<p>A big selling point is the seller's documented maintenance history. According to the listing:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>HVAC replaced</strong> in June 2023</li>\n<li><strong>New water heater</strong> in 2024</li>\n<li><strong>RO system with UV light</strong> and a <strong>new kitchen sink and faucet</strong> in 2025</li>\n<li>New <strong>chair-height toilets</strong> in both bathrooms in 2022</li>\n<li><strong>New garage door</strong> in 2021</li>\n<li>Metal fence on the front walkway in 2018</li>\n<li>Water softener installed in 2015</li>\n<li><strong>New roof</strong> in 2013 and exterior paint in 2007</li>\n<li>Preventive Terminix treatment for the last 15 years</li>\n</ul>\n<p>With the HVAC and water heater recently replaced, a buyer avoids two of the largest near-term costs in an Arizona home. The roof is now about 13 years old, so it deserves a close look during the inspection.</p>\n\n<h2>Outdoor Space and Potential</h2>\n<p>The fenced lot has <strong>low-maintenance desert landscaping</strong> and a <strong>cozy covered patio</strong> with <strong>mountain and fountain views</strong>. The listing notes there is <strong>room to add a pool or a guest casita</strong>. Because there is no HOA, adding one is mainly a matter of town permits and setbacks, not association approval. That opens up options for added value, rental income or space for extended family.</p>\n\n<h2>Living in Fountain Hills</h2>\n<p>Fountain Hills sits on the northeast edge of the Valley, surrounded by the McDowell Mountains and Sonoran Desert preserve land. It is known for its quiet, small-town character and for the fountain itself, one of the tallest in the world, which shoots from the lake in <strong>Fountain Park</strong>.</p>\n<p>This home is only <strong>3 to 5 minutes from Fountain Park</strong> and the downtown dining and shopping district. Residents also enjoy:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hiking and biking in the <strong>McDowell Mountain Regional Park</strong> and the Fountain Hills preserve trails</li>\n<li>Recognition as an International <strong>Dark Sky Community</strong>, with outstanding stargazing</li>\n<li>Golf courses, community events, and the annual art festivals downtown</li>\n<li>Easy access to Scottsdale via Shea Boulevard, and to the Verde River and Saguaro Lake for weekend outings</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Is It a Good Value?</h2>\n<p>At $465,000, this home works out to about <strong>$340 per square foot</strong>, an entry point into a town where many homes list well above $600,000. The listing notes that a nearby home on the same street, 13845 Kendall, <strong>recently sold for $645,000</strong>. Every property differs in size, condition and features, so that sale is not a direct comparison, but it suggests room for appreciation, especially for a buyer who adds a pool or casita over time. No HOA dues also lowers your monthly cost of ownership.</p>\n\n<h2>Buy With Attorney and Paralegal Oversight</h2>\n<p>At Camelback Home Group, every purchase is supported by <strong>attorney and paralegal oversight</strong>. We review your contract, the seller's disclosures, the title commitment and any recorded deed restrictions, which matters even when there is no HOA. If you plan to add a pool or casita, we can help you understand the issues before you close so there are no surprises.</p>\n\n<h2>Schedule a Showing</h2>\n<p>Under-$500K homes with no HOA in Fountain Hills do not last long. To tour 13825 N Kendall Drive, call Camelback Home Group at <strong>(480) 203-3039</strong> or reach out online. We will arrange a showing, prepare a comparable-sales analysis, and help you make a confident, well-protected offer.</p>"
