    "content": "<h2>A Former Model Home in Charleston Estates</h2>\n<p>Former model homes are built to impress, and <strong>22176 E Estrella Road</strong> in Queen Creek delivers on that promise. Located in the sought-after <strong>Charleston Estates</strong> community, this move-in-ready single-level home offers <strong>3 bedrooms, 2.5 bathrooms, a den, and 2,496 square feet</strong> of thoughtfully upgraded living space. Built in 2013 and listed at <strong>$719,850</strong>, it pairs builder showcase finishes with a backyard made for Arizona living and a rare <strong>three-car garage</strong>.</p>\n<h2>A Welcoming Arrival</h2>\n<p>Your first impression begins at a <strong>custom iron gate</strong> that opens to a shaded front courtyard with a large seating area. It is the perfect place for morning coffee or evening conversation with neighbors, and it sets the tone for the quality you will find inside.</p>\n<h2>Inside the Home</h2>\n<p>Step inside to a spacious <strong>formal dining room</strong> and a light-filled great room with large windows and a <strong>gas fireplace</strong>. The open layout flows naturally into the kitchen, which is designed for people who love to cook and entertain:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Quartz countertops</strong> and an island with seating</li>\n<li>A <strong>double oven</strong> and gas cooktop</li>\n<li>A walk-in pantry for abundant storage</li>\n<li>An eat-in kitchen dining area in addition to the formal dining room</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The split floor plan places the primary suite apart from the secondary bedrooms for added privacy. The primary retreat includes a large ensuite bath with a <strong>walk-in shower, separate soaking tub, two vanities</strong>, and a deep walk-in closet. Bedrooms two and three share a hall bath and feature updated carpet and paint. A den with <strong>custom bookshelves</strong> makes an ideal home office, library, or reading room.</p>\n<p>Practical touches round out the home, including a laundry room with built-in cabinets, nine-foot-plus ceilings, ceiling fans, and a garage setup that includes a two-car garage and a separate one-car garage, both with <strong>epoxy flooring</strong>. The extra bay is perfect for storage, a workshop, or a golf cart.</p>\n<h2>Resort-Style Backyard</h2>\n<p>Out back, the low-maintenance yard is designed for both relaxing and entertaining. A <strong>built-in BBQ area</strong>, synthetic grass, and a spacious patio create an outdoor living room you can enjoy for much of the year without the upkeep of natural turf.</p>\n<h2>Life in Queen Creek</h2>\n<p>Queen Creek has become one of the most desirable communities in the Southeast Valley, blending an agricultural heritage with modern convenience. This home sits just minutes from local favorites like <strong>Queen Creek Olive Mill</strong> and <strong>Schnepf Farms</strong>, along with Costco, Frontier Family Park, and the <strong>Queen Creek Wash trail system</strong> for walking, running, and biking.</p>\n<p>Travelers will appreciate the short drive to <strong>Phoenix-Mesa Gateway Airport</strong>, and the town's planned new downtown district promises even more restaurants, shopping, and entertainment in the years ahead. Highly rated schools, wide-open spaces, and a strong sense of community continue to draw families to the area.</p>\n<h2>Market Context: Is It a Good Value?</h2>\n<p>At $719,850, this home comes in at roughly <strong>$288 per square foot</strong>. For a single-story home with a three-car garage, model-home upgrades, a den, and a finished low-maintenance backyard, that pricing is competitive within Queen Creek's established neighborhoods. Comparable new construction often requires buyers to spend significantly more to add window coverings, landscaping, a BBQ island, and garage finishes, all of which are already in place here.</p>\n<h2>Attorney-Backed Representation</h2>\n<p>Buying a home is one of the largest financial decisions you will ever make. At Camelback Home Group, every client benefits from <strong>attorney and paralegal oversight</strong> on their transaction at no extra cost. Our team reviews contracts, HOA disclosures, inspection responses, and title documents with legal precision, so you can move forward with confidence.</p>\n<h2>Schedule a Showing Today</h2>\n<p>Former model homes in Charleston Estates do not come along often. To see <strong>22176 E Estrella Road, Queen Creek, AZ 85142</strong> in person, <strong>call Camelback Home Group at (480) 203-3039</strong> or <a href=\"/#contact\">contact us online</a> to schedule your private showing.</p>"
