    "excerpt": "A spacious 5-bedroom, 3-bath Festival Foothills home on a corner lot with White Tank Mountain views, a main-level guest suite, an upstairs loft and a 3-car garage. Listed at $475,000 — roughly $151 per square foot in one of North Buckeye's most amenity-rich communities.",
    "metaDescription": "26107 W Potter Drive in Buckeye's Festival Foothills — a 5-bed, 3-bath, 3,146 sq ft corner-lot home with mountain views and a 3-car garage, listed at $475,000.",
    "content": "<h2>Space, Mountain Views and a Corner Lot in Festival Foothills</h2><p>If you have been searching the West Valley for a home with real room to grow, <strong>26107 W Potter Drive in Buckeye</strong> deserves a close look. This two-story residence in the Festival Foothills community offers <strong>3,146 square feet of living space, five bedrooms, three full bathrooms and a three-car garage</strong>, all on a corner lot with no neighbors to the east. Listed at <strong>$475,000</strong>, it delivers the kind of square footage that is increasingly hard to find at this price point anywhere in metro Phoenix.</p><p>Built in 2007, the home sits in North Buckeye with wide-open space and sweeping views of the White Tank Mountains. It's a setting that feels removed from the bustle of the city while still keeping you connected to everyday conveniences.</p><h2>Inside the Home: A Layout That Works for Real Life</h2><p>The main level is built around an <strong>open-concept living area</strong> finished in a neutral color palette, with recessed can lighting, wood-look flooring, white trim and white doors. It's a clean, versatile backdrop that makes it easy to bring your own style without having to undo someone else's.</p><p>The kitchen opens to the living space and features ceramic tile flooring, stainless steel appliances, a kitchen island, an eat-in area and a pantry. One of the most practical features of this floor plan is the <strong>main-level bedroom and full bath</strong>, ideal for guests, multigenerational living, a live-in relative or a quiet home office.</p><p>Upstairs, the home continues to deliver:</p><ul><li><strong>A bright loft</strong> with plenty of natural light, perfect for a media room, play space or second living area</li><li><strong>A split-bedroom floor plan</strong> that gives the primary suite added privacy</li><li><strong>A spacious primary bedroom</strong> with a bath featuring double sinks, a separate shower and tub, and a walk-in closet</li><li><strong>Three additional bedrooms</strong>, each with a ceiling fan, served by a full bath</li><li><strong>An upstairs laundry room</strong> with a sink and wall-to-wall storage cabinets</li></ul><p>Other highlights include 9-foot-plus flat ceilings, central air with programmable thermostats, natural gas heating and high-speed internet availability. The <strong>three-car garage</strong> gives you room for vehicles, a workshop, or the storage that active households always seem to need.</p><h2>A Backyard Ready for Your Vision</h2><p>The backyard is a blank canvas. Whether you dream of a pool, a covered patio with an outdoor kitchen, raised garden beds or simply a low-maintenance desert landscape, you have the flexibility to create the outdoor space that fits your lifestyle. Being on a corner lot with no neighbors to the east adds a sense of openness that many interior lots can't match.</p><h2>Life in Festival Foothills and North Buckeye</h2><p>Festival Foothills is one of North Buckeye's most family-friendly master-planned communities. Residents enjoy a <strong>large 12-acre park with sports fields</strong>, splash pads, a playground and walking trails, all set against the backdrop of the White Tank Mountains. It's the kind of neighborhood where weekend mornings mean a walk on the trails and evenings bring desert sunsets over the mountains.</p><p>Buckeye itself has been one of the fastest-growing cities in the United States, and that growth has brought new shopping, dining, schools and health care to the West Valley. From Festival Foothills, you're roughly <strong>15 minutes from the Loop 303 freeway</strong>, which connects you to Surprise, Peoria, Goodyear and the broader Phoenix metro. Outdoor lovers will appreciate being <strong>less than 45 minutes from Lake Pleasant Regional Park</strong>, with boating, fishing, hiking and camping, and the White Tank Mountain Regional Park trail system is close by as well.</p><h2>Market Context: Is This a Good Value?</h2><p>At $475,000 for 3,146 square feet, this home comes in at roughly <strong>$151 per square foot</strong>, which is a compelling number in today's metro Phoenix market. Comparable square footage in the East Valley or central Phoenix often carries a significantly higher price tag. For buyers who prioritize space, such as growing families, multigenerational households, or anyone who needs a dedicated home office, five bedrooms plus a loft at this price is a rare combination.</p><p>Buckeye's continued expansion, including new commercial development and ongoing infrastructure investment along the 303 corridor, positions the area well for long-term growth. Buying in an established community like Festival Foothills, with its parks and amenities already in place, means you get the benefits of that growth without living in the middle of an active construction zone.</p><h2>Buy With Legal Oversight on Your Side</h2><p>At <strong>Camelback Home Group</strong>, every transaction is backed by <strong>attorney and paralegal oversight</strong> through our affiliation with Camelback Law Group. From reviewing the purchase contract and HOA documents to tracking inspection and due-diligence deadlines, our team makes sure the details are handled correctly so you can focus on finding the right home. It's an added layer of protection that most traditional brokerages simply don't offer.</p><h2>Schedule Your Showing Today</h2><p>Homes with this much space, a corner lot and mountain views at this price don't stay on the market long. If 26107 W Potter Drive sounds like the right fit, <strong>contact Camelback Home Group at (480) 203-3039</strong> to schedule a private showing or ask any questions about the property, the Festival Foothills community or the Buckeye market. We would be glad to help you take the next step toward your new home.</p>"
